        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2a6b7bac-02bc-5659-8d00-f073f9dc5ad0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Moominpappa at Sea, The Old Man and the Sea, Moominvalley in November, Who Will Comfort Toffle?\n- People: Tove Jansson, Ernest Hemingway\n- Topics: Moomin series, literary reference, publication\n\nFacts:\n- The Old Man and the Sea is a short novel by Ernest Hemingway that he wrote in 1951 in Bimini, Bahamas, and it was published in 1952.\n- Moominpappa at Sea has an original title that loosely references Ernest Hemingway's novel The Old Man and the Sea, but that reference is not reflected in translation.\n- Moominvalley in November is set contemporaneously with Tove Jansson's 1965 novel Moominpappa at Sea.\n- Moominvalley in November is the only installment in the Moomin series in which the titular Moomin family are absent.\n- Who Will Comfort Toffle? is the second picture book in the Moomin series by Tove Jansson.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
